{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22787 - PROTEIN:6147",
  "verbalization": "Khrinone C is implicated in the regulation of Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Khrinone C acts as a target of multiple compounds, which in turn target the SDR family member 9. Specifically, Khrinone C directly interacts with a sialyltransferase enzyme, which is a target of 2-Methylheptyl propanoate and (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan. These compounds, in turn, are targets of the SDR family member 9. This chain of interactions implies that Khrinone C may influence the activity of the SDR family member 9 through the activation or inhibition of these downstream targets. The evidence supports a mechanism where Khrinone C indirectly affects the SDR family member 9 by modulating the activity of its target enzymes, highlighting a potential role in metabolic or enzymatic regulation.",
